common --enable_bzlmod
# The server exits 10 minutes after its last command, not the 3-hour default: on 2026-10-12 fourteen idle
# gate servers held the host at full swap (github-8f's report). A tick's gates run minutes apart, so ten
# minutes keeps the warm cache through a tick and frees the heap after it.
startup --max_idle_secs=600
test --test_output=errors --test_summary=terse
# nemik:W2221 (operator 2026-11-16, relayed by github-cb: "Not streaming to build buddy, even if not
# using a gate, is a bug."): every bazel run streams to BuildBuddy, so a scratch run has an invocation
# id to read per-target durations from (the bes-logs skill). The two addresses are the directory's
# answers (luthen-observability checks/endpoints_query.py grpc-bes and http-web, --side host, as_of
# 2026-11-16T12:21:55Z and 12:22:02Z), the same shape mtools and eight other repos carry; re-ask the
# directory before editing them, and do not copy them from another repo's file.
build --bes_backend=grpc://buildbuddy-bes.buildbuddy.svc.cluster.local:1985
build --bes_results_url=http://buildbuddy-web.buildbuddy.svc.cluster.local:8080/invocation/
